        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a84eefab-fcc6-565f-8e67-762c88090718",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Hibiscus waimeae, H. arnottianus, Hawaiian hibiscus, Urera kaalae\n- Places: Hawaii, Oʻahu, Molokaʻi\n- Concepts: Native species, flower color, habitats, associated plants\n\nFacts:\n- Hawaiian hibiscus are seven species of hibiscus regarded as native to Hawaii.\n- H. arnottianus of Oʻahu and Molokaʻi and H. waimeae are the only Hawaiian hibiscuses that have white flowers.\n- H. waimeae inhabits coastal mesic, mixed mesic, and wet forests at elevations of 250 meters and above.\n- Urera kaalae is associated with maile (Alyxia oliviformis), hame (Antidesma platyphyllum), Asplenium kaulfusii, Athyrium species, and ʻāwikiwiki (Canavalia species).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
